# 33. NO MOCK PRODUCTION CONTRACT

The following are forbidden in production:

- fake projects
- fake users
- fake deployment URLs
- fake billing status
- fake authentication
- fake AI success
- fake generated files
- fake analytics
- fake production metrics

Mocks may exist only in explicitly isolated development/testing
contexts.

---

# 34. NO DEAD UI CONTRACT

Every visible production action must have a real purpose.

Forbidden:

- dead buttons
- dead navigation
- fake toggles
- fake deployment buttons
- fake settings
- fake billing controls
- fake file actions

If functionality is not implemented, the interface must not
misrepresent it as operational.

---

# 35. CHANGE CONTROL

After implementation begins, changes must be categorized.

## CATEGORY A — BUG FIX

Does not change intended product behavior.

Can be fixed directly.

---

## CATEGORY B — IMPLEMENTATION IMPROVEMENT

Improves performance, maintainability or reliability without
changing the product contract.

Can be implemented after verification.

---

## CATEGORY C — PRODUCT CHANGE

Changes:

- UX
- page structure
- navigation
- workflow
- feature behavior
- visual system

Requires documentation review before implementation.

---

## CATEGORY D — ARCHITECTURAL CHANGE

Changes:

- backend architecture
- authentication architecture
- database architecture
- deployment architecture
- AI architecture
- core frontend architecture

Requires explicit architecture review.

---

